(   voltage source V_L is active, driving current into terminal A. Since the internal network is) Tj
T*
(   purely resistive, the input impedance seen by V_L is Rth. The current flowing out of terminal A) Tj
T*
(   is -V_L / Rth.) Tj
T*
(   - Combining both contributions via superposition:) Tj
T*
(   I_L = I_sc - V_L / Rth = I_sc - \(I_L * RL\) / Rth.) Tj
T*
(   - Under open circuit \(RL -> infinity, I_L = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   0 = I_sc - V_oc / Rth => V_oc = I_sc * Rth. Define Vth = V_oc.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute I_sc = Vth / Rth back into the current equation:) Tj
T*
(   I_L = Vth / Rth - \(I_L * RL\) / Rth => I_L * \(1 + RL / Rth\) = Vth / Rth => I_L * \(Rth + RL\) =) Tj
T*
(   Vth.) Tj
T*
(   - Thus: I_L = Vth / \(Rth + RL\), which represents a series loop of source Vth, internal) Tj
T*
(   resistance Rth, and load RL.) Tj
T*
