/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove the Maximum Power Transfer Theorem for DC resistive circuits, and determine the efficiency at maximum power.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Maximum Power Transfer Theorem for DC Circuits:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement:) Tj
T*
(   Maximum power is delivered from an active linear DC source network \(represented by Thevenin) Tj
T*
(   equivalent Vth and Rth\) to a variable load resistance RL when the load resistance equals the) Tj
T*
(   source Thevenin resistance: RL = Rth.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Load current: I_L = Vth / \(Rth + RL\).) Tj
T*
(   - Instantaneous power consumed by load RL:) Tj
T*
(   P_L\(RL\) = I_L^2 * RL = [Vth / \(Rth + RL\)]^2 * RL = \(Vth^2 * RL\) / \(Rth + RL\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   - To find the condition for maximum power, differentiate P_L with respect to RL and set) Tj
T*
ET

