(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the mathematical transformation formulas for Delta-to-Star and Star-to-Delta resistor conversions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Delta-Star \(Pi-Tee\) Transformations:) Tj
T*
(   1. Delta-to-Star Conversion:) Tj
T*
(   - Let Delta resistors connected between terminals \(1, 2, 3\) be R12, R23, R31.) Tj
T*
(   - Let equivalent Star resistors radiating from central neutral node N to terminals 1, 2, 3 be) Tj
T*
(   R1, R2, R3.) Tj
T*
(   - Equating terminal resistances across pairs with the third terminal open:) Tj
T*
(   Across 1-2: R1 + R2 = R12 || \(R23 + R31\) = [R12 * \(R23 + R31\)] / \(R12 + R23 + R31\).) Tj
T*
(   Across 2-3: R2 + R3 = R23 || \(R31 + R12\) = [R23 * \(R31 + R12\)] / \(R12 + R23 + R31\).) Tj
T*
(   Across 3-1: R3 + R1 = R31 || \(R12 + R23\) = [R31 * \(R12 + R23\)] / \(R12 + R23 + R31\).) Tj
T*
(   - Solving this linear system by subtracting pairs yields:) Tj
T*
(   R1 = \(R12 * R31\) / \(R12 + R23 + R31\).) Tj
T*
(   R2 = \(R12 * R23\) / \(R12 + R23 + R31\).) Tj
T*
(   R3 = \(R23 * R31\) / \(R12 + R23 + R31\).) Tj
T*
(   - Rule: Star resistor at node k equals the product of the two adjacent delta resistors divided) Tj
T*
(   by the sum of all three delta resistors.) Tj
T*
(   2. Star-to-Delta Conversion:) Tj
T*
(   - Compute pairwise products of star resistors: R1*R2 + R2*R3 + R3*R1.) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting delta expressions and simplifying gives:) Tj
T*
(   R12 = R1 + R2 + \(R1 * R2\) / R3.) Tj
T*
(   R23 = R2 + R3 + \(R2 * R3\) / R1.) Tj
T*
(   R31 = R3 + R1 + \(R3 * R1\) / R2.) Tj
T*
(   - Rule: Delta resistor between nodes i and j equals the sum of the two connected star resistors) Tj
T*
(   plus their product divided by the opposite star resistor.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
