(   - Let [A] be the \(N-1\) x B reduced incidence matrix of the network graph.) Tj
T*
(   - By KCL, the branch currents satisfy: [A] * [i_b] = [0].) Tj
T*
(   - By KVL, the branch voltages are related to node voltages [v_n] by: [v_b] = [A]^T * [v_n].) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluate total instantaneous power:) Tj
T*
(   Sum_{k=1}^B \(v_k * i_k\) = [v_b]^T * [i_b].) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute [v_b]^T = \([A]^T * [v_n]\)^T = [v_n]^T * [A]:) Tj
T*
(   Sum_{k=1}^B \(v_k * i_k\) = [v_n]^T * \([A] * [i_b]\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since [A] * [i_b] = [0] by KCL:) Tj
T*
(   Sum_{k=1}^B \(v_k * i_k\) = [v_n]^T * [0] = 0.) Tj
T*
(   3. Universality of Tellegen's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   - The proof relies exclusively on network topology \(incidence matrix [A]\), KCL, and KVL.) Tj
T*
(   - It makes NO assumption about branch constitutive relationships \(Ohm's law\).) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, it is valid for linear, non-linear, passive, active, time-invariant, and) Tj
T*
(   time-varying networks.) Tj
