(   [Problem Statement]: State and explain the Superposition Theorem, detailing its scope, proof, and why it cannot be directly applied to power.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Superposition Theorem in Linear Systems:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement:) Tj
T*
(   In any linear bilateral electrical network containing multiple independent sources, the voltage) Tj
T*
(   across \(or current through\) any branch is the algebraic sum of the voltages \(or currents\)) Tj
T*
(   produced by each independent source acting alone, with all other independent sources) Tj
T*
(   deactivated.) Tj
T*
(   - Deactivation protocol: Replace independent voltage sources with short circuits \(0 V\) and) Tj
T*
(   independent current sources with open circuits \(0 A\). Dependent sources must remain fully) Tj
T*
(   active.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Basis:) Tj
T*
(   - Linear systems satisfy the principle of superposition: L\(a*x1 + b*x2\) = a*L\(x1\) + b*L\(x2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Network equations in matrix form: [G] * [V] = [I_s1] + [I_s2] + ... + [I_sk].) Tj
T*
(   - Because matrix inversion is linear:) Tj
T*
(   [V] = [G]^-1 * [I_s1] + [G]^-1 * [I_s2] + ... = [V]_source1 + [V]_source2 + ...) Tj
T*
(   3. Non-Applicability to Power Calculations:) Tj
T*
(   - Electrical power is a quadratic function of voltage or current: P = I^2 * R = V^2 / R.) Tj
T*
(   - If two sources act together: I_total = I1 + I2.) Tj
T*
(   - Total power: P_total = \(I1 + I2\)^2 * R = \(I1^2 + I2^2 + 2*I1*I2\) * R = P1 + P2 + 2 * I1 * I2) Tj
T*
(   * R.) Tj
T*
(   - Because of the cross-product term \(2 * I1 * I2 * R\), power is non-linear and cannot be found) Tj
T*
(   by summing individual powers: P_total != P1 + P2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
