(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Millman's Theorem and demonstrate how it simplifies parallel generator branches into an equivalent source.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Millman's Theorem and Parallel Generator Reduction:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theorem Statement:) Tj
T*
(   When n voltage sources V1, V2, ..., Vn having internal series resistances R1, R2, ..., Rn are) Tj
T*
(   connected in parallel across common terminals A and B, they can be reduced to a single) Tj
T*
(   equivalent voltage source V_eq in series with resistance R_eq:) Tj
T*
(   - V_eq = \(Sum_{k=1}^n V_k * G_k\) / \(Sum_{k=1}^n G_k\), where G_k = 1 / R_k is the branch) Tj
T*
(   conductance.) Tj
T*
