(   - R_eq = 1 / \(Sum_{k=1}^n G_k\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Analytical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Let terminals A and B be open-circuited. Choose terminal B as the reference node \(0 V\) and) Tj
T*
(   let the potential of terminal A be V_AB.) Tj
T*
(   - Apply KCL at node A:) Tj
T*
(   Sum_{k=1}^n I_k = 0 => Sum_{k=1}^n \(V_AB - V_k\) / R_k = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Expand summation:) Tj
T*
(   V_AB * Sum_{k=1}^n \(1 / R_k\) - Sum_{k=1}^n \(V_k / R_k\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Since G_k = 1 / R_k:) Tj
T*
(   V_AB * Sum\(G_k\) = Sum\(V_k * G_k\) => V_AB = [Sum\(V_k * G_k\)] / [Sum\(G_k\)].) Tj
T*
(   - This terminal open-circuit voltage is V_eq.) Tj
T*
(   - To find internal resistance R_eq, deactivate all independent sources \(V_k = 0\). The parallel) Tj
T*
(   combination of all conductances yields:) Tj
T*
(   G_eq = Sum_{k=1}^n G_k => R_eq = 1 / G_eq.) Tj
