/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State the Compensation Theorem and explain its application in sensitivity analysis and bridge circuits.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Compensation Theorem in Electrical Networks:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement:) Tj
T*
(   If the resistance of any branch in a linear active network carrying current I is altered by an) Tj
T*
(   incremental amount delta-R, the resulting changes in currents and voltages throughout the) Tj
T*
(   entire network are identical to those produced by an ideal compensating voltage source V_c) Tj
T*
(   placed in series with that branch, where:) Tj
T*
(   V_c = I * delta-R opposing the original branch current.) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Original branch voltage: V = I * R.) Tj
T*
(   - When resistance becomes R' = R + delta-R, new current is I' = I + delta-I.) Tj
T*
(   - New branch voltage: V' = I' * \(R + delta-R\) = I' * R + I' * delta-R.) Tj
T*
ET

