(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the concept of Duality in electrical circuits, listing dual pairs and steps to construct a dual network graph.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Duality in Electrical Circuit Theory:) Tj
T*
(   1. Principle of Duality:) Tj
T*
(   Two networks are duals if the mathematical loop equations of one network have the identical) Tj
T*
(   algebraic form as the node equations of the second network.) Tj
T*
(   2. Dual Parameter Pairs:) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage \(v\) <-> Current \(i\)) Tj
T*
(   - Resistance \(R\) <-> Conductance \(G = 1/R\)) Tj
T*
(   - Inductance \(L\) <-> Capacitance \(C\)) Tj
T*
(   - Loop / Mesh <-> Node / Cut-set) Tj
T*
(   - Series connection <-> Parallel connection) Tj
T*
(   - KVL \(Sum V = 0\) <-> KCL \(Sum I = 0\)) Tj
T*
(   - Short circuit \(V = 0\) <-> Open circuit \(I = 0\)) Tj
T*
(   - Thevenin equivalent <-> Norton equivalent) Tj
T*
(   - Impedance \(Z\) <-> Admittance \(Y\)) Tj
T*
(   3. Graphical Construction of Dual Network:) Tj
T*
(   - Place a dot \(dual node\) inside each mesh of the original planar network.) Tj
T*
(   - Place an additional reference dot \(datum/ground node\) in the outer infinite region.) Tj
T*
(   - Connect the dots of adjacent meshes by dashed lines passing through each shared branch.) Tj
T*
(   - Replace each crossed branch with its dual element \(e.g., a crossed 5 Ohm resistor becomes a 5) Tj
T*
(   Siemens conductor; an inductor becomes a capacitor\).) Tj
T*
(   - Assign source polarities according to circulating mesh conventions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
