(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the fundamental matrices in Network Graph Theory: Incidence matrix [A], Tie-set matrix [B], and Cut-set matrix [Q].) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Network Graph Theory and Topological Matrices:) Tj
T*
(   1. Graph Fundamentals:) Tj
T*
(   - For a connected graph with N nodes and B branches:) Tj
T*
(   - Tree: A connected subgraph containing all N nodes and no closed loops. Number of tree) Tj
T*
(   branches \(twigs\) = N - 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Co-tree: Complement of tree. Number of links \(chords\) = B - \(N - 1\) = B - N + 1.) Tj
T*
(   2. Incidence Matrix [A]:) Tj
T*
(   - Dimension: N x B \(or reduced \(N-1\) x B by eliminating datum node\).) Tj
T*
(   - Elements a_ij = +1 if branch j leaves node i; -1 if branch j enters node i; 0 if branch j is) Tj
T*
(   not connected to node i.) Tj
T*
(   - KCL formulation: [A] * [I_b] = [0].) Tj
T*
(   - KVL relation: [V_b] = [A]^T * [V_n].) Tj
T*
(   3. Fundamental Tie-Set Matrix [B_f]:) Tj
T*
