(   [Problem Statement]: Solve a bridge circuit: Calculate Thevenin equivalent across load terminals of an unbalanced Wheatstone bridge.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Analytical Solution of an Unbalanced Wheatstone Bridge:) Tj
T*
(   1. Circuit Specification:) Tj
T*
(   - Bridge excited by DC voltage source V_s = 20 V connected between top node A and bottom node) Tj
T*
(   B.) Tj
T*
(   - Left branch: R1 = 20 Ohms \(top\), R3 = 30 Ohms \(bottom\). Intermediate node C.) Tj
T*
(   - Right branch: R2 = 40 Ohms \(top\), R4 = 10 Ohms \(bottom\). Intermediate node D.) Tj
T*
(   - Load resistor RL is connected across terminals C and D.) Tj
T*
(   2. Step 1: Open-Circuit Thevenin Voltage \(Vth = V_CD\):) Tj
T*
(   - With RL removed:) Tj
T*
(   Potential at node C \(voltage divider\): V_C = V_s * [R3 / \(R1 + R3\)] = 20 * [30 / \(20 + 30\)] =) Tj
T*
(   20 * 0.6 = 12 V.) Tj
T*
(   Potential at node D \(voltage divider\): V_D = V_s * [R4 / \(R2 + R4\)] = 20 * [10 / \(40 + 10\)] =) Tj
T*
(   20 * 0.2 = 4 V.) Tj
T*
(   - Thevenin voltage: Vth = V_C - V_D = 12 V - 4 V = 8.0 V.) Tj
T*
(   3. Step 2: Thevenin Resistance \(Rth seen between C and D\):) Tj
T*
(   - Deactivate independent source V_s \(short-circuit source terminals A and B\):) Tj
T*
(   Resistors R1 and R3 are in parallel between node C and ground: R_C = R1 || R3 = \(20 * 30\) / \(20) Tj
T*
(   + 30\) = 600 / 50 = 12 Ohms.) Tj
T*
(   Resistors R2 and R4 are in parallel between node D and ground: R_D = R2 || R4 = \(40 * 10\) / \(40) Tj
T*
(   + 10\) = 400 / 50 = 8 Ohms.) Tj
T*
(   - Total Thevenin resistance: Rth = R_C + R_D = 12 Ohms + 8 Ohms = 20.0 Ohms.) Tj
T*
(   4. Load Current and Power for RL = 60 Ohms:) Tj
T*
(   - I_L = Vth / \(Rth + RL\) = 8 V / \(20 + 60\) = 8 / 80 = 0.1 A \(100 mA\).) Tj
T*
(   - Power in load: P_L = I_L^2 * RL = \(0.1\)^2 * 60 = 0.60 W \(600 mW\).) Tj
T*
