(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Temperature Coefficient of Resistance, deriving formulas for resistance variation and temperature rise in conductors.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Temperature Coefficient of Resistance and Thermal Calculations:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Origin:) Tj
T*
(   - In metallic conductors \(e.g., copper, aluminum\), electrical conduction is mediated by free) Tj
T*
(   electron transport. As temperature rises, lattice ions vibrate with larger thermal amplitudes,) Tj
T*
(   increasing electron-phonon scattering and reducing electron mean free path and drift velocity.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - For moderate temperature ranges:) Tj
T*
(   R\(T2\) = R\(T1\) * [1 + alpha_1 * \(T2 - T1\)], where alpha_1 is the temperature coefficient of) Tj
T*
(   resistance at reference temperature T1 \(units: 1 / deg C\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Temperature Coefficient at Different Temperatures:) Tj
T*
(   - The temperature coefficient is itself temperature-dependent:) Tj
T*
