(   [Problem Statement]: Solve an active circuit problem containing a Voltage-Controlled Voltage Source \(VCVS\) using Nodal Analysis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Active Circuit Solution with VCVS via Nodal Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Circuit Description:) Tj
T*
(   - A DC circuit contains independent voltage source V_s = 12 V connected between node 1 and) Tj
T*
(   ground.) Tj
T*
(   - Resistor R1 = 4 Ohms connects node 1 to node 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Resistor R2 = 6 Ohms connects node 2 to ground.) Tj
T*
(   - A VCVS of value 3*V_x is connected between node 2 and node 3, where V_x is the voltage across) Tj
T*
(   R2 \(V_x = V2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Resistor R3 = 2 Ohms connects node 3 to ground.) Tj
T*
(   2. Analysis at Node 2 and Supernode \(2-3\):) Tj
T*
(   - Notice that the VCVS is connected between node 2 and node 3, forming a Supernode!) Tj
T*
(   - Constraint equation: V3 - V2 = 3 * V_x.) Tj
T*
(   - Since V_x = V2 - 0 = V2:) Tj
T*
(   V3 - V2 = 3 * V2 => V3 = 4 * V2.) Tj
T*
(   3. Supernode KCL Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - Sum of currents leaving supernode enclosing nodes 2 and 3:) Tj
T*
(   \(V2 - V1\) / R1 + V2 / R2 + V3 / R3 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute numerical values \(V1 = 12 V, R1 = 4, R2 = 6, R3 = 2\):) Tj
T*
(   \(V2 - 12\) / 4 + V2 / 6 + V3 / 2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply entire equation by 12 to clear fractions:) Tj
T*
(   3 * \(V2 - 12\) + 2 * V2 + 6 * V3 = 0 => 3*V2 - 36 + 2*V2 + 6*V3 = 0 => 5*V2 + 6*V3 = 36.) Tj
T*
(   4. Solve System:) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute V3 = 4 * V2:) Tj
T*
(   5 * V2 + 6 * \(4 * V2\) = 36 => 5 * V2 + 24 * V2 = 36 => 29 * V2 = 36.) Tj
T*
(   - V2 = 36 / 29 = 1.241 V.) Tj
T*
(   - V3 = 4 * \(36 / 29\) = 144 / 29 = 4.966 V.) Tj
T*
(   - Controlling voltage V_x = 1.241 V; VCVS output = 3.724 V.) Tj
T*
