T*
(   3. Equivalent Circuit Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - The total circuit reduces to series resistor R1 in series with the parallel combination of) Tj
T*
(   shunt resistor R2 and R_in:) Tj
T*
(   R_in = R1 + [R2 * R_in] / \(R2 + R_in\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Quadratic Solution:) Tj
T*
(   - Clear denominator by multiplying through by \(R2 + R_in\):) Tj
T*
(   R_in * \(R2 + R_in\) = R1 * \(R2 + R_in\) + R2 * R_in.) Tj
T*
(   R_in^2 + R2 * R_in = R1 * R2 + R1 * R_in + R2 * R_in.) Tj
T*
(   R_in^2 - R1 * R_in - R1 * R2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Applying the quadratic formula \(taking the positive root since resistance must be positive\):) Tj
T*
(   R_in = [ R1 + sqrt\(R1^2 + 4 * R1 * R2\) ] / 2.) Tj
T*
(   5. Special Case \(R1 = R2 = R\):) Tj
T*
(   - R_in = [ R + sqrt\(R^2 + 4 * R^2\) ] / 2 = R * [ 1 + sqrt\(5\) ] / 2 = 1.61803 * R \(Golden Ratio) Tj
T*
(   phi * R\).) Tj
