T*
(   2. Formulation of MNA:) Tj
T*
(   - Partition circuit unknowns into:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) N-1 Node voltages [v].) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Currents through independent and dependent voltage sources [i_v].) Tj
T*
(   - The system is cast into block matrix form:) Tj
T*
(   [ G B ] [ v ] = [ i_s ]) Tj
T*
(   [ C D ] [ i_v ] [ e_s ]) Tj
T*
(   - Matrix [G]: Standard nodal conductance matrix formed by passive resistors/conductances.) Tj
T*
(   - Matrix [B]: Topological incidence matrix routing voltage source currents into nodes.) Tj
T*
(   - Matrix [C]: Links node voltages to voltage source branch equations \(for independent sources,) Tj
T*
(   C = B^T\).) Tj
T*
(   - Matrix [D]: Accounts for dependent voltage source couplings \(zeros for independent sources\).) Tj
T*
(   - Vector [i_s]: Independent current sources entering nodes.) Tj
T*
(   - Vector [e_s]: Values of independent voltage sources.) Tj
T*
(   3. Algorithmic Advantage:) Tj
T*
(   - Guaranteed non-singular matrix for physically realizable circuits, easily assembled via) Tj
T*
(   element 'stamps' in computer code \(SPICE\).) Tj
