/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss Non-Linear DC Circuit Analysis using the Load-Line Method and Newton-Raphson numerical iteration.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Analysis of Non-Linear DC Circuits:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Nature:) Tj
T*
(   - When a network contains non-linear devices \(diodes, varistors\) where i = f\(v\), linear) Tj
T*
(   superposition and simple matrix inversion fail.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Graphical Load-Line Method:) Tj
T*
(   - Isolate the non-linear element from the linear network, replacing the linear network with its) Tj
T*
(   Thevenin equivalent \(Vth, Rth\).) Tj
T*
(   - Terminal equation: V = Vth - I * Rth => I = \(Vth - V\) / Rth \(Load Line, straight line with) Tj
T*
(   slope -1/Rth\).) Tj
T*
(   - Device characteristic: I = f\(V\) \(e.g., Shockley diode equation I = Is * [exp\(V/n*Vt\) - 1]\).) Tj
T*
(   - The intersection of the load line and device V-I curve uniquely identifies the Quiescent) Tj
T*
(   Operating Point \(Q-point: V_Q, I_Q\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Newton-Raphson Iterative Numerical Method:) Tj
T*
(   - Define error function: g\(V\) = \(Vth - V\)/Rth - Is * [exp\(V/n*Vt\) - 1] = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Iteration formula:) Tj
T*
(   V^{\(k+1\)} = V^{\(k\)} - g\(V^{\(k\)}\) / g'\(V^{\(k\)}\).) Tj
T*
(   - Derivative: g'\(V\) = -1/Rth - \(Is / n*Vt\) * exp\(V/n*Vt\) = - \(G_th + g_d\), where g_d is the) Tj
T*
(   dynamic small-signal conductance.) Tj
T*
(   - Converges quadratically in 3 to 5 iterations in modern circuit simulators.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
