(   - Series lattice arm impedance: Z_a = Z_oc/2 or Z_sc/2 depending on open/short conditions.) Tj
T*
(   - Specifically:) Tj
T*
(   Z_a is the input impedance of one half-network with all bisected connecting lines) Tj
T*
(   OPEN-CIRCUITED \(even excitation\).) Tj
T*
(   Z_b is the input impedance of one half-network with all bisected connecting lines) Tj
T*
(   SHORT-CIRCUITED \(odd excitation\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Proof Outline via Even and Odd Mode Decomposition:) Tj
T*
(   - Any arbitrary excitation at port 1 \(V1\) and port 2 \(V2\) can be decomposed into:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Even mode: V_e = \(V1 + V2\)/2 applied to both ports \(no current crosses symmetry plane ->) Tj
T*
(   Open Circuit bisection\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Odd mode: V_o = \(V1 - V2\)/2 applied anti-symmetrically \(voltage is zero at symmetry plane) Tj
T*
(   -> Short Circuit bisection\).) Tj
T*
(   - Input impedances in even and odd modes correspond directly to lattice arms Z_a and Z_b.) Tj
T*
(   3. Utility:) Tj
T*
(   - Drastically simplifies the design and analysis of symmetric bridge-T filters, crystal) Tj
T*
(   filters, and attenuators.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
