(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the conditions for zero current in the galvanometer of an Anderson Bridge and a Kelvin Double Bridge.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Bridge Null Conditions for Low and Moderate Resistances:) Tj
T*
(   1. Kelvin Double Bridge \(Low Resistance Precision Measurement\):) Tj
T*
(   - Designed to eliminate lead and contact resistances in measuring low resistances \(< 1 Ohm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Incorporates two sets of ratio arms: outer ratio arms \(P, Q\) and inner ratio arms \(p, q\),) Tj
T*
(   with connecting lead resistance 'r'.) Tj
T*
(   - Balance Condition Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   Galvanometer potential difference V_G = 0 yields:) Tj
T*
(   R = \(P / Q\) * S + [ \(p * r\) / \(p + q + r\) ] * [ \(P / Q\) - \(p / q\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - By precisely matching the ratios P/Q = p/q:) Tj
T*
(   The second term vanishes identically, giving:) Tj
T*
