12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the principle and operation of a Negative Impedance Converter \(NIC\) and its circuit implementation using an Op-Amp.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Negative Impedance Converter \(NIC\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Principle and Definition:) Tj
T*
(   - An active two-port device that transforms a positive load impedance Z_L connected at port 2) Tj
T*
(   into a negative impedance Z_in = -k * Z_L at port 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Current Inversion NIC \(INIC\): V1 = V2, I1 = k * I2 \(reverses current direction\).) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage Inversion NIC \(VNIC\): V1 = -k * V2, I1 = -I2.) Tj
T*
(   2. Op-Amp Implementation of INIC:) Tj
T*
(   - An ideal op-amp with resistor R1 from inverting terminal to ground, feedback resistor R2 from) Tj
T*
(   output to inverting terminal, and resistor R from output to non-inverting terminal.) Tj
T*
(   - Connect load impedance Z_L between non-inverting terminal and ground.) Tj
T*
(   - Input voltage V_in is applied to non-inverting terminal:) Tj
T*
(   V+ = V_in. Due to negative feedback, V- = V_in.) Tj
T*
(   Current through R1: I_R1 = V_in / R1.) Tj
T*
(   Op-amp output voltage: V_out = V_in * \(1 + R2 / R1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Current entering non-inverting terminal through resistor R:) Tj
T*
(   I_in = \(V_in - V_out\) / R = [V_in - V_in * \(1 + R2 / R1\)] / R = - V_in * \(R2 / R1\) / R.) Tj
T*
(   - Input Impedance:) Tj
T*
(   Z_in = V_in / I_in = - R * \(R1 / R2\).) Tj
T*
(   - For R1 = R2: Z_in = -R.) Tj
T*
(   3. Application:) Tj
T*
(   - Used to cancel unwanted parasitic series resistance in telecommunication transmission lines) Tj
T*
(   and build active filters and oscillators.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
